 "customerTurns": 4,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "My Dyson V10 Absolute (SV12) won't run at all now. On the battery display there's a red light flashing when I press the trigger, then nothing. It was charging overnight. Do I need a new battery or is the whole thing dead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't confirm what RED LIGHT FLASHI means on your model, so I'll go by what it is doing. From what you have described, the most likely cause is the battery or charger. Check the charger is in a working socket and pushed fully into the vacuum (or dock), and wipe the charging contacts clean and dry. The charging light should come on. Was the charger, socket or contacts the problem (and is it sorted), does the charging light never come on, or is the charger fine with the light on?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "The charger light is on and I tried a different socket (the hallway one) with the same result. The contacts look clean too. Blue lights come on while it's charging, but it still flashes red when I press the trigger."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Charge it fully and use it on the normal mode. Is it running for its normal time now, or still short?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "It's not running at all, so there's no runtime to measure. The motor won't start on any mode and it's still flashing red once a second when I press the trigger. For the last few weeks before this it only managed about 8 minutes on the lowest mode. The battery isn't swollen, hot or smelly, if that matters."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Switch it off and unplug it (or take the battery off) first. I can't confirm what FLASHING RED ONC means on your model, so I'll go by what it is doing. Detach the wand and floorhead and look through each part, and check the bin inlet — a coin dropped through the wand should fall straight out. Did you find a blockage and clear it, is there one you can't shift, is a hose split, or was it all clear?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I've checked the filter and bin already: filter washed last month, bin empty, no blockages. I haven't taken the wand and floorhead apart to look through them, but the motor doesn't even try to start, so I doubt it's a blockage. Is it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: battery — flat or failed (cordless)]\nIt is likely the battery has failed, given the recent drop in runtime and the current inability to run. You should replace the battery pack. The checks point to the battery — flat or failed (cordless). I could not find a confirmed match for model V10 ABSOLUTE (SV12) in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  }
 ],
